BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-AM68x-ALPHA3                    2024-06-28
=============================================================

- Linux TI vendor kernel v6.1.80 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.009)
  * Tag: v6.1.80-09.02.00.009-phy3
- U-Boot v2023.04 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.009)
  * Tag: v2023.04-09.02.00.009-phy1
- Yocto 4.0 (kirkstone)

NOTE:
This is an ALPHA release and has not been tested for full functionality. It is
possible that some features are not working or stable. This release will NOT
be supported after the first full BSP release.


Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------

- phytec-headless-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-3
- phytec-qt5demo-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-3


Build Environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 20.04 64-bit

New Features:
-------------

- VDD_CPU_AVS support

Issues fixed:
-------------

- The MIPI DSI interface has the RGB colors flipped occasionally
- The display backlight PWM is not set to the default value occasionally
- Low eth0 bandwidth was observed on several boards
- Kernel hanging due to R5 cores powering up in wrong order

Known Issues:
-------------

For phyboard-izar-am68x-1:
- MMC/SD is limited to 3.3v
- The MCU ethernet is limited to 100 MBit/s and booting is not possible
  due to a phy reset triggered from the MCU domain which is unknown to Linux

For all:
- The eMMC is limited to HS200 speed mode
- The PWM fan is set to 0 when the SoC temperature is exceeding 70° during boot
  time. As workaround set the max duty cycle to 254 in /etc/fancontrol
